  "prefLabel": "Stra 1104.01 New Hampshire Scholar Designation",
  "priorExpiration": "2018-07-02",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Stra 1104.01 New Hampshire Scholar Designation. Eligible students who are determined by their awarding postsecondary institution to be on track to receive a New Hampshire scholar designation in the second semester of their senior year of high school shall be considered to have earned the New Hampshire scholar designation for purposes of a scholarship award. If an eligible student who is awarded a scholarship of $2,000.00 per year fails to earn the New Hampshire scholar designation, that student’s scholarship shall be reduced to $1,000.00 per year and the remaining funds shall revert to the governor’s scholarship fund.\n\nSource. #12446, INTERIM, eff 1-3-18, EXPIRES: 7-2-18; ss by #12550, eff 6-19-18 (formerly Stra 1104.02)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/stra1100.html"
